Chapter: Channel
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A Channel is a record containing buffer for fixed-size circular storage, capacity for the maximum number of messages, write-pos and read-pos as slot indices, count for the number of messages currently buffered, and closed as a flag set after closing.

 A SendResult is a record containing sent, True when the message was accepted, and chan, the channel state after the send attempt.

 A RecvResult is a record containing value, a Maybe with the received message or None when empty, and chan, the channel state after the receive attempt.

 To chan-create gives Channel a, allocating a new channel with the given capacity filled with zero placeholders.
 To chan-try-send gives SendResult a, writing a message into the buffer when the channel is open and not full.
 To chan-try-recv gives RecvResult a, reading the next message from the buffer when available.
 To chan-close gives Channel a, marking the channel as closed; no further sends succeed after closing.
 To chan-is-empty gives Boolean, True when no messages are buffered.
 To chan-is-full gives Boolean, True when count equals capacity.
 To chan-is-closed gives Boolean, True when the channel has been closed.
 To chan-size gives Integer, the number of messages currently buffered.

 We say:

Section: Types

  Channel a = record {
    buffer : List a,
    capacity : Integer,
    write-pos : Integer,
    read-pos : Integer,
    count : Integer,
    closed : Boolean
  }

  SendResult a = record {
    sent : Boolean,
    chan : Channel a
  }

  RecvResult a = record {
    value : Maybe a,
    chan : Channel a
  }

Section: Construction

  chan-create : Integer, a -> Channel a
  chan-create (capacity) (zero) =
    Channel {
      buffer = chan-fill capacity zero 0 [],
      capacity = capacity,
      write-pos = 0,
      read-pos = 0,
      count = 0,
      closed = False
    }

  chan-fill : Integer, a, Integer, List a -> List a
  chan-fill (cap) (zero) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= cap then acc
    else chan-fill cap zero (i + 1) (list-push acc zero)

Section: Send

  chan-try-send : Channel a, a -> SendResult a
  chan-try-send (ch) (msg) =
    if ch.closed then SendResult { sent = False, chan = ch }
    else if ch.count >= ch.capacity then SendResult { sent = False, chan = ch }
    else SendResult {
      sent = True,
      chan = Channel {
        buffer = list-set-at (ch.buffer) (ch.write-pos) msg,
        capacity = ch.capacity,
        write-pos = int-mod (ch.write-pos + 1) (ch.capacity),
        read-pos = ch.read-pos,
        count = ch.count + 1,
        closed = False
      }
    }

Section: Receive

  chan-try-recv : Channel a -> RecvResult a
  chan-try-recv (ch) =
    if ch.count == 0 then RecvResult { value = None, chan = ch }
    else RecvResult {
      value = Just (list-at (ch.buffer) (ch.read-pos)),
      chan = Channel {
        buffer = ch.buffer,
        capacity = ch.capacity,
        write-pos = ch.write-pos,
        read-pos = int-mod (ch.read-pos + 1) (ch.capacity),
        count = ch.count - 1,
        closed = ch.closed
      }
    }

Section: Close and Query

  chan-close : Channel a -> Channel a
  chan-close (ch) = Channel {
    buffer = ch.buffer,
    capacity = ch.capacity,
    write-pos = ch.write-pos,
    read-pos = ch.read-pos,
    count = ch.count,
    closed = True
  }

  chan-is-empty : Channel a -> Boolean
  chan-is-empty (ch) = ch.count == 0

  chan-is-full : Channel a -> Boolean
  chan-is-full (ch) = ch.count >= ch.capacity

  chan-is-closed : Channel a -> Boolean
  chan-is-closed (ch) = ch.closed

  chan-size : Channel a -> Integer
  chan-size (ch) = ch.count

